    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91350.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "All right, good morning. Welcome to the show with his Thursday, December 16th. Got a lot to talk about today, plus our guest in studio later this morning. Congressman Neil Dunn is gonna be here, and we have got a lot of questions that have not only off of the top of my head, But submitted from you guys to ask the congressman. We're gonna have a great conversation with him later this morning. We got, like I said, a lot of questions that you guys wanna know. I've got a lot of questions for him. He's got a few things he wants to talk about as well. So that'll be coming up later on this morning during the seven o'clock hour. We'll have him in studio, which I'm looking forward to because this means we're not gonna be distracted. by, you know, a tight schedule, which is usually the case when we get most of our congressmen and senators and everybody on the air. They've always got these tough schedules, so we got a little more freedom, so this is going to be good conversation, so I'm looking forward to that. Also, just to give you a heads up that there was an accident reported already this morning. We're off to a great start, folks. and slow it down a little bit. But coming off the halfway right there at Wildwood Road, there is an accident reported with injuries. No road blocks or anything, and not a lot of traffic going through there right now. But if you are coming over the halfway heading towards a bridge right there at Wildwood Road, there was an accident that was reported. So just be careful on that. Also continuing today, US 231 and Transmitter Road, they are still working on those railroad tracks. So you may find It a little bit difficult to get through that area this morning again. Anyhow, good morning. Thank you so much for tuning in today. Boy, we, like I said, we got some stuff to talk about and some things that are just going to make people go, whoa, there's some new news about the January 6th. And we talked about a lot of the tweets and the messages and the text message and everything else going back and forth. Wait, do you hear this? This is gonna fire you up this morning. We're gonna talk about that. Plus, like I said, the congressman will be on with us this morning too. And tomorrow, I'm looking forward to this. We've had this guy on the air before, and he's a lot of fun. And we all know how much Donald Trump has been attacked. by social media and banned and all this other stuff. We've had this kid on before. His name is Victor Nieves. And he goes by Datboy Victor. That's his online handle. And this kid has been probably blocked more times. Not only by Instagram and Facebook and censored, but also TikTok and a few others as well. And honestly, it has happened to him more than it has to Donald Trump. It just hasn't been a complete permanent black, but he's had to create, I don't even know, I can't keep track of how many new profiles he has to create. And you would think to yourself, oh my God, what is this kid doing? You know, how horrible of a person is he to constantly get blocked like that? Well, he's not. He's not all that bad. As a matter of fact, he just gets on there and he talks about some of the regular issues that are going on in the world, talks about his thoughts and opinions on abortion, not wild, crazy conspiracy theories. Just, hey, you know, this is what the law says about this. This is what My faith and religion says about it, and this is what I think. It talks about guns and the Second Amendment, what the Second Amendment is about. And he talks about other things with the Constitution as well. So he's not like some wild radical that is out there spreading misinformation and encouraging violence or anything along that line. And yet he is constantly, and I mean constantly, being censored on social media. And this is becoming something that's kind of a danger. And we're seeing it all the time. And now Twitter with their new tyrant of a leader that they have, they're not going to be penalizing users who claim that people who are vaccinated against coronavirus can still spread the disease. So they want to get you for spreading misinformation, but then when you actually spread information that is confirmed information, they're going to penalize you for doing that. This is Twitter. This is the social media world that we're living in with all of this censorship. And at some point, this censorship has got to stop. It really truly has because this is not going to create a good environment for this to be happening. And even though the official guidelines from the Center for Disease Control claims opposite of what Twitter says, they are going to penalize you for if you spread that information. So apparently, this new jack wipe over there at Twitter that is now running things, he knows better than the CDC. So if you go out there and tweet something that says, hey, the Center for Disease and Prevention and Control, you know that federal agency says that people who have the vaccination can still spread the COVID virus. You're gonna get penalized for it. I'm not kidding. I wish this was a joke, but it's really not. But Twitter said that when tweets include misleading information about COVID-19, we may place a label on those tweets that includes corrective information about that claim. I would like to know where they're going to put a collective information about a claim that says, hey, the Center for Disease Prevention and Control says that it can still spread it if you are vaccinated. I mean, what is this going to be like, you know, Facebook with their fact checkers? You know, the fact checkers that don't like your opinion. So they fact check it with their opinion. But their website also notes that a section detailing its rules about COVID-19 misinformation and saying that we may apply labels to tweets that contain, for example, false or misleading claims that people who have received the vaccine can spread or shed the virus or symptoms or immunity to unvaccinated people. We all know that the only way that the, uh, the, uh, the Aramicon virus or the variant could have gotten here to the U S from South Africa was when the fully vaccinated man, the first case in the U S flew back from South Africa, fully vaccinated flew back from Africa, uh, and got the variant. And then from there, we've seen, you know, many other cases popping up everywhere. And we are seeing more and more medical evidence that shows that yes, a vaccinated person can still carry and spread the coronavirus. I love it. I love our social media with how they are so much more informed than you and I. And my question is, what is the agenda of people like Twitter when they do something like that? And of course Joe Biden in an interview on Tuesday, apparently he didn't get the memo from Twitter because in this this interview President Joe Biden falsely claimed that people who were vaccinated from coronavirus could not spread the disease. But the CDC says that you can. And he says everybody talks about freedom, about not to have a shot or to have a test. Well, guess what? How about patriotism? How about you make sure you're vaccinated so you do not spread the disease to anybody else? What about that? What's the big deal? The big deal, Joey, is you have no right to tell me what to do simply because you may be the President of the United States, but I'm still your boss. You do not. get to dictate what I get to do and do not do to my own body. And if you don't like it, you can stuff your head in a toilet and flush it. And I don't care if you're the president of the United States, because that's the way you can have it. You do not get to tell me, my family, my friends, my neighbors, my coworkers, my enemies, my Democrat friends, liberal friends, conservative friends, independent friends, religious friends, atheist friends, you don't get to tell any of us what to do. And more of Washington needs to get that through their thick skulls that you bunch of clowns work for us. So how about that one, Joey? Go suck on that for a while. What's the big deal? The big deal is that you are telling us that we have to put something into our bodies. That is not the government's role to do that. It's not the government's role to tell the people what to do. And it is, we are far past due for us to be correcting the federal government on who's actually in charge. First off, the states don't answer to the federal government. The federal government answers to the states. And the state governments don't answer to the federal government. They answer to we the people. We the people are the boss. We hire you to do the government business, not hire you to tell us what to do. Get it through your thick skull. But he continued on saying that those who aren't vaccinated are the ones that continue to spread the disease. And we should think of as patriotic duty just to get that shot. Meanwhile, the CDC and other scientists and medical professionals have proven that vaccinated people still spread the disease. Which at this point, we're hearing all of this talk about the romecon virus, or the variant of it, and how it's not bad. Even Dr. Fauci had said, yeah, well, it's not as bad as we were thinking it was going to be, it's just mild symptoms. Even Dr. Fauci, the guy that none of us trust because he does nothing but lie to us, even he is on board with what all the medical professionals in South Africa and here in the US who is our treating some of the people with this variant are saying, well, it's not that bad. Otherwise put as it is starting to show signs. If you go past all of this BS that we're getting from the mainstream media and from some of our politicians and from some of these social media groups, if you get past all of that, you will see that the reality is, is that the coronavirus is starting to fade out. It'll probably never go away. I mean, let's be honest about that. It'll probably never go away. It'll be probably like the flu, something that'll just be popping up here and there. But we're already at a variant that is weak enough to just say it's mild symptoms. And yet we have places like California and New York City that have instituted the new or re-instituted the policies of having to have a mask. You got to be masked up indoors everywhere. Even though science has also proven, I mean, we got to use that horrible science. If science has proven that these masks that we wear, whether they're a cotton mask or these paper surgical mask or whatever it is that we're wearing, does not block coronavirus from going past the mask. Science has proven that. I mean, it's like trying to throw a football down the center of a football field and not touch the out of bounds lines. Not a very difficult thing. Same thing. And this is coming from science. This is not somebody just going, well, you know what? This is what I think it is. Science has proven that. But Joe Biden, he's continuing on and he said that what asked if he would back down on his federal vaccine mandates after they were held up in the courts, Biden said that he will keep pursuing them. And he says, I'm going to continue to fight these in court. And he also repeated his argument that the pandemic was only affecting the unvaccinated. Again, pay attention, dude. There are vaccinated people like the one that brought the romecon here to America that are sick with it. We said this is a pandemic of the unvaccinated, not the vaccinated, the unvaccinated. That's the problem. The problem that we have with the sheep that are allowing people like you and Nancy Pelosi and all these other idiots in Washington that think they know better than the rest of us. That's the problem. Those people there, they're the problem. Not the unvaccinated. So you can kiss my rosy Irish Scottish little booty there, Joey. That's all I got to say to that. I'm already heated up this morning. Anyhow, more of the stupidness coming out of the Biden administration, it doesn't stop today. It really doesn't. We've got so much plus coming up later on this morning. We do have Congressman Neil Dodd is going to be in the studio. We have a lot of questions to ask him. I've already compiled my list from you guys, let alone the list of stuff that I've got. So hang on 2, 3, 3, 9, 9, 8, that is also the number to get on the show today. A lot of other damning information for the Democrats coming up too in a bit. We've got to take a break. We'll be right back. This is the bride rush show on News Talk at 101. Good morning.",
