    "turn_text": "and this administration turned around and flew these two people back to the United States after Donald Trump had them deported is ridiculous. And before his deportation, Claudio Rojas, who had lived at his illegal alien for 19 years, was deported in 2018 following more than a decade here in the US. I'm sorry, but dude, you were here illegally, you had to go. Sorry, not your country. And these people got to realize that this is the rule at almost every single nation in the world. You cross their borders, one, if you do it illegally, you might even get shot in some of them. Or you're going to go to jail. They're not going to be like, oh, you broke our laws and came into our country. And now you want to tell us what to do with our country? Oh, come here. Give me a big hug. You know what? You need a place to live. Yeah, how about a steak dinner? You want to steak dinner? Come on, let's go get you something to eat. Oh, those clothes don't look good. How about some clothes? You got any money on you? Well, here, here, take some money. What else would you like? You're not going to find a nation in the world that is going to do that. You will be detained at pretty much every nation in the world when you illegally cross their border. But here we are, we have somebody that has been deported from the country because they were here illegally. And now claiming that the Customs and Border Enforcement is retaliating against these people because of their open borders advocacy. You know what, stuff it. Seriously, just stuff it. You're from another country. Don't care what you think about our border policy. Don't really care. And if you were here illegally and you were doing advocacy to encourage and open borders into somebody else's country that you're illegally here, screw you. You should not have been flown back in here. But this is what the Biden administration did. And it goes to show just how dangerous this administration is and how much they don't care about you. They don't care about American citizens at all. And it's obvious that they don't care. And Rod DeSantis was down in Wildwood yesterday. And he blasted the critical race theory and the less pursuit of wokeness, making it clear that Florida will not tolerate cultural Marxism. deeming it an elite driven phenomenon. The governor went on the defense on the offense as he was introducing the Stop Rongs to our Kids and Employees Act or Stop Woke Act, halting the advancement of the Marxist ideology in Florida schools and places of employment. The governor said that we want all of our students to understand why was our country founded. What are some of the key ideas that made us different? And he noted the Founding Fathers belief that mankind was endowed by our Creator with rights, emphasizing these rights did not come from government. And he said, I think that when you see now the rise of this woke audiology is an attempt to really delegitimize our history, delegitimize our institutions. And I view the wokeness as cultural Marxism. And of course, we know that the leftists are embracing the ideology to seek the alternate way of life and change the very fabric of the society that we are living in and the culture that we have here in the US. Because we're such a bad, horrible country. And that's the reason for why so many people want to come to for years, want to come to the free America. The America that is free from government control. Well, not so much anymore. But that's why these people wanted to come here. And yet the left, their wokeism, which I don't care if they get upset that we use that because that's their word, their definition, we're going to use it. Oh my God, I'm so offended by the fact that you use woke, shut up, sit down, be quiet, let the adults speak for a minute. But DeSantis briefly walked through some of the instances of a CRT being taught in the schools across the nation. You remember the CRT that is not being taught, that is a myth that is something that's made up that the Republicans are saying, even though you have, you know, superintendents of schools and principals and other teachers and everybody else saying that yes, we do teach this. But the left, when I go on the defense on that to like, no. CRT made up. That's the Republicans. That's Donald Trump. But Governor DeSantis included the Arizona Department of Education's toolkit. That suggests that babies and toddlers show signs of racism. Which I'm sorry, I want to know what idiot actually did that study and decided that that was the case. Because I want to punch you in the face. I really do. I know that violence is not always the answer, but sometimes you're just so stupid you need to be punched in the face. Just to rattle whatever little brains you've got up there around to maybe show that something works up there. And we all know that racism is not something that you were just simply born with. You learn it from others. I mean, how many times have you seen two little kids who just don't care what color the skin is? They're best buds because they don't know. They don't care. It's a fellow human being. That's my size. And the whole idea, the thing that toddlers and babies are showing signs of racism, it shows that you're an idiot. It really, truly does. And he said that this is a nationwide problem. The governor emphasized explaining that he has a responsibility in Florida not to teach CRT as it violates his Sunshine State's standards. While the State's Department of Education approved a proposal effectively banning CRT and the content inspired by it in the schools, Rhonda Santa said, we need to do more to make sure these moves carry weight. And that is what he hopes that the Florida legislation will do with the Stop Woke Act in the next session. But in addition to that, this is not something that we just need to have legislation to stop. We saw this in Loudon County. This is Loudon County, Virginia, is where a lot of this started. And I'm telling you that the revolution in this country, to take it back from these wokest idiots, is starting in the school systems, and that is where the fights got to continue. And even here in Bay County, we can't just sit back and go, okay, well, we're in Bay County, so everything should be okay. No. as parents and as community people, community leaders, and just people in the community, we should be involved. Because even if you don't have children, and even if your children are grown up and gone, what gets taught in our schools will affect our community. And it may not be something that is taught right now in Bay County schools. But how do you know unless you are being engaged? How do you know unless you are going to a school board meeting and asking, hey, is this stuff being taught? And you know what, in addition to that, we also have to talk to when you are not a parent, talk to the parents and say, hey, what are your concerns? What are you seeing your children being taught? We all need to get together on that. And that is something that we need to push as a fight. And that's again, that's not just something here in Bay County. I mean, we haven't, I have heard that there have been a couple of things that are a little questionable, but we are not anywhere near as bad as all these other places around the country that are in these, these woke leftist areas. But we have to pay attention to it. We can't just let it go. And on top of that, even if Nothing is going on like that in Bay County schools. If we the people, because remember, our school board is elected by us. And the school board is the one that oversees the schools. Even the superintendent, we elect the superintendent. If we continue to put pressure on everybody, and it doesn't have to be in there going in there and trying to be some jerk and making stuff up, no, just go in there and say, hey, I just want to let you know I'm watching and we want to make sure that we are not doing something that's going to damage the future of our children and the future of our community. And you let them know we're watching. This way they know and also future school board members, future superintendents, future principals and teachers in our system know that we the people are watching. and that we will not tolerate our children being indoctrinated by something down that road. We just got to make sure that it doesn't happen. And of course, this is also stuff that we need to continually push on all elected leaders, that we have to make sure that we are communicating with them. And I know that one of the complaints that I hear all the time is that I try and call Congressman Dunn. I try and call Senator Scott. I try and call Senator Rubio. I try to call Congressman Gates or I try to call one of our representatives and don't ever get to talk to them. Something that you have to know too is that there's a system that is in place that granted I am not to fully defend the elected officials for not always being there to talk with the people. But there are systems that are in place to be able to take your criticism, your concerns, your anger, and whatever else it might be, and compile that information so that the representatives know. So the information does get to them, but it doesn't get to them unless we make the contact. And we can just send letters if we want, but making the phone calls also is something important, even if it's just a staff member you talk to. And I know that some people have said, hey, I've tried calling Congressman Dunn's office and getting no response. Well, you know what, I'll ask Congressman Dunn about that just because that's one of the questions that has been asked. But we have to make sure that we are letting our public officials know They work for us and that we have concerns. And if we continue to just live our lives and forget about it, what's going to happen is what we're seeing. We're going to see this cultural Marxism where things sneak up behind us because we're not paying attention. So the more that we pay attention, the better that we are. And thank God we do have a governor like Ron DeSantis who is on top of this. And hopefully the CRT is something that will not happen here in the state of Florida as we push against this. But the legislation that the governor is pushing would protect employees, teachers and school staff and ultimately students and families. He announced this during his press conference yesterday in Wildwood and under the legislation, CRT would be considered an unlawful employment practice. making it clear that corporations and public sector employers violate the Florida Civil Rights Act when they subject their employees to training that espouses race or sex stereotyping or scapegoating, including critical race theory. It also considers CRT to be discriminatory in the realm of education. and stopping what the governor's office has described as indoctrination in guys of professional development and requires districts and schools to adhere to professional development frameworks consistent with the Florida laws and publicly adopted state standards. The measures would satisfy the Florida Board of Education's previous actions making them law to guard students against the indoctrination curriculum. So while we can say let's go Brandon, we can also say let's go Big Daddy D in the meaning that it's actually supposed to be. Thank God we've got Ron to sand us on our side because we need more governors and more leaders to be just like that. Hang on. We got to take a quick little break here in a second. But you know what? If you if you are looking to take care of some of the problems with your home, if you've got those high utility bills or you got like walk into your house, you get those cold spots, hot spots here. Check this out. Call my friends over at Kuala installation of Panama City. Jeff and Rhonda, they're the owners. They're locals. They're natives. They they're also vets, by the way. So it's a veteran owned company. They