d ride. We're talking about the January 6th insurrection investigation. James Carville, who is the big Democrat strategist, he said yesterday on MSNBC's The Beat that Americans should strap in because the House like committee investigating the January 6 riot at the Capitol will expose former President Donald Trump was behind the massive criminal act. The massive criminal act. And I hope we're not talking about the insurrection, because that wasn't really much of an insurrection. And you would think that by now, if there was actual plans for an insurrection, that somebody, somebody on the ground who was not an actual Trump staffer or advisor or something, that, you know, that average Joe Schmo would say, hey, I was told by Donald Trump or I was told by Mark Meadows or I was told by somebody that came over from the White House that what we have to do is go and attack the White House. So we were told to go or the Capitol, we had to attack the Capitol. Nobody has done that. So far there has been absolutely no evidence of anybody being told that this is what we need to do. We need to go attack the Capitol building. Has anybody seen it? Anyone? I mean, I haven't missed that, have I? I mean, the Democrats are saying that Donald Trump said to go attack the Capitol building. No, he didn't. He said, let's go up there and let them know that we're here. Peace fully. He used that P word. And I don't know, maybe, maybe peaceful. Of course then again, we got to take into consideration all the, the Antifa and BLM riots that were peaceful demonstrations. Oh yeah, we're, we're here, we're here in Minnesota and we're at this peaceful riot. What, the building behind me on fire? No, it's, it's all peaceful. It's a little cold out here. So they, they lit a fire to stay warm. As we kind of learned that the word peaceful according to Democrats means, go burn that thing and kick somebody in the face. Us on this side of the aisle, we always considered peaceful as being, well, peaceful. I mean, do I have to look up the definition of peaceful? Just for the Democrats so they can, I'll do it, hang on, we'll do it. Definition, whoops, I gotta spell that right. Hang on, peaceful, not peach fuzz. Why would never mind? I don't want to know. Okay, here, we'll get the actual definition of peaceful, just so that we we're all on the same page here, Demi's. The definition of peaceful is from a free from disturbance tranquil, not involving war or violence. Okay. So, so now that we got that definition from Oxford, everybody, everybody got that one? You need to stop and write it down. Peaceful, especially their Dems, if you're, if you're listening, write it down. Peaceful means one of two examples here, free from disturbance and tranquil. and not involving war or violence. So again, Donald Trump says to his followers at the rally, let's peacefully go up there to the Capitol building and let them know we're here. Again, where is the evidence? that says, hey, let's do an insurrection. Let's go attack the Capitol building, hunt down Mike Pence, and hang him in the Capitol building, and then just go beat everybody up. That's not there. But Carvel went on saying that it was a massive criminal act, that the people who penetrated the Capitol were criminals. The people who helped them penetrate the Capitol were criminals. And he said to the anchor, you're a lawyer, you know this. If I drive the getaway car or I cause or in case the place out, I'm as guilty as the triggerman. That's the way the law operates. So can we talk about maybe the Antifa and BLM members that posted on their social medias which got taken down? Let's go and actually infiltrate the Trump rally. Can we talk about them? Can we for a second? Maybe. Can we also talk about the fact that little old radio talk show hosts like me about a year ago now, roughly, I was talking about the reports that were coming out about the fact that Antifa and BLM was posting on their social media that they're going to infiltrate the Trump rallies. And meanwhile, the Capitol Police and the FBI and everybody else and the Dems up there on the Capitol will be like, we didn't even know this was going to happen. We knew nothing. Liars. absolute punch of liars. But James Carville saying, you know, strap in America, because this House Select Committee is investigating Donald Trump is going to, they're going to expose Donald Trump with all of those big lies. And the fact that he was, he was the mastermind behind this criminal act. And of course, we talked about this the other day, the text messages and the tweets that were going on that were described during the hearing. And of course, Adam Schiff, he's the one that said, hey, well, walk here. Here's a bunch of text messages that were from Donald Trump and from between Mark Meadows and in the Fox News people. And he went off and read them. Well, there's a few people that said, oh, hold up, wait a second, hang on, that doesn't really jive, that doesn't, no. Well, it's now been confirmed that the January 6 committee has admitted that it doctored Republican text message in Adam Schiff's presentation. The House Select Committee on the January 6 attack admitted yesterday that it had doctored a text message cited by Representative Adam Pencil next shift in his push on Monday to hold the former White House Chief of Staff Mark Meadows in contempt. The Federalist Sean Davis first reported this Wednesday morning that shift had manipulated the text message, cutting out the full context and adding punctuations into it, which he falsely implied was authored by a Republican lawmaker. Breitbart News summarized this one. One message which shift attributed to the Republican lawmaker was doctored to read quote-unquote on January 6, 2021, comma, Vice President Mike Pence, comma, as president of the Senate, comma, should call out all electoral votes that he believes are unconstitutional as no electoral votes at all. Period. But the original message came back from former Department of Defense Inspector General Joseph Schmitz, who had drafted the summarized legal arguments that Representative Jim Jordan forwarded to Meadows, and Schiff led out the full exchange, which read, on January 6, 2021, Vice President Mike Pence as president of the Senate, should call out all the electoral votes that he believes are unconstitutional, as no electoral votes at all. in accordance with the guidance from Founding Father Alexander Hamilton and the Justice Prudence. No legislative at wrote Alexander Hamilton in the federalist number 78, contrary to the Constitution, can be valid. The court in Hubbard v. Lowell reinforced this truth that an unconstitutional statute is not a law at all as is a proportion no longer open to discussion. Well, Adam Schiff kind of omitted that important part in there because it what didn't fit the narrative. And in his statement on the on-screen graphics shift, erased the final two paragraphs and the final clause of the first paragraph of the text message before inserting punctuations that was never there, all without disclosing what he had done. Now the question is, is there going to be any punishments or anything? No. But Wednesday afternoon, the Federalist reported that the January 6 committee admitted that it had manipulated the text. So if they manipulated that text message, who's to say they didn't manipulate the others? And how can we trust these guys to continue on with this investigation? And of course Liz Cheney was mocked as Mark Meadows text suggests that there was no insurrection plot. This Cheney was mocked by the conservatives on Monday evening after a hearing of the select committee on the January 6 attack produced text messages from former White House Chief of Staff Mark Meadows that showed numerous people close to then President Donald Trump, including Don Jr., were surprised by the Capitol riot and reached out to him and issued a statement against it, which he then did. The panel voted to recommend that