t we had that in 2020 over and over and over again. And it wasn't just one place. It was in Pennsylvania. It was in Michigan. It was in, you know, in Georgia. It was in Nevada. It was in Arizona. All over the place we saw this. And it was at the very least enough to say, ooh, something doesn't look right. 2016, let's just face it, you lost. And yet they went on and on for four years bashing Donald Trump, bashing Donald Trump supporters, claiming that the election was stolen and that we really truly won. With no evidence, no potential evidence, nothing to point at other than, I feel that we should have won and we didn't get our way. And meanwhile, the 2020 election had more evidence and more, at least on the surface proof, that something didn't go right somewhere. Now again, I've said this all along. That yes, Joe Biden may have legitimately won this election. By 10 million votes? No. By maybe a million or two, maybe. But this is what we keep getting from the left. And how are we supposed to trust them when they come out with their final report on January 6? The Democrats are so scared that they are going to lose power in control. And everything, even the Democrats' strategists are saying, yeah, 2022, forget it, guys, it's over. You cannot bounce back from this one. But they keep pushing harder and harder and harder on the narrative. They're pushing harder and harder on COVID. Got to scare the people. scare the people and make the Republicans look bad. Those horrible Republicans, they're trying to kill you all and we're here to protect you from what? From the mild variant that everywhere that has the variant is saying, yes, it's spreading faster, but all the symptoms are mild. Okay, it's winter time. What do we always get in the winter? The flu? How often does that spread around? It does. What kind of symptoms do you have? Generally mild? And yet the Democrats are out here trying to scare the living hell out of everybody that you're all gonna die, put your mask back 