    "turn_text": "welcome back to the show. Thanks so much for listening. Coming on the top of the hour, we got Congressman Neil Dunn that'll be joining us on the show. And we got a lot to talk with him about including the Build Back Better Act, Build Back Better Broke, President Biden's eight gazillion trillion dollar plan that he's got going on. Well apparently the plan looks like it's going to be dead until 2022 and Joe Biden is not going to get his way when it comes to you know getting it on the on done by Christmas time. That's what his plan was was to have it done by Christmas, but it's not looking like that's going to happen. The Democrat leadership has now desperately tried to win Manchin's vote to pass the largest welfare package since Lyndon Johnson's great society back in the 1960s. But Joe Manchin is really kind of one of the big hold-ups behind it and saying, no, this isn't going to happen. And of course he had a interaction the other day with some of the, the mainstream reporters when he basically told them, you know, your BS and this is BS. And Manchin and the Republicans have voiced worries that spending trillions of dollars in welfare during the 40 year high inflation would hurt the economy. The congressional budget officer, the CBO estimated Friday that the price of the package would double Biden's estimate. Senator Mitch McConnell said that on Wednesday and anyone who with a shred of sense knows that this is absolutely wrong time to unleash a multi-trillion dollar taxing and spending spree. Every single day brings new evidence our Democrat colleagues should give the country a break. And I think there needs to be a lot more reviewing this and checking to see if this is really, truly good. Every time we turn around, of course, remember this package is like 2,500 pages? 2,500 pages that I'm almost sure that nobody has read entirely by themselves. And that every time we turn around, we're finding new things that are hidden in this. I've yet to completely read the entire thing, but everything that I have read in it, and sometimes it's just, it's a half a paragraph or half a page, one paragraph, and it's something that you just kind of look at and go, wow, that shouldn't be in there. And yet it is. And anyone, uh, you know, who's really kind of supporting this probably shouldn't be. And we need to do something about it. Two, three, three, nine, eight, that is the number for the show. Good morning. Welcome to the Brian Rush show.",
