    "turn_text": "All right, welcome back to the show. Thank you so much for listening coming up the top of the hour. We do have Congressman Neil Dunne that's going to be joining us in the studio. It's going to be a great conversation. I know that there's a lot of questions that people have. I got some questions. He's got some answers. And he's also going to fill us in on some of the things that he's been working on up in Washington. So we're going to talk with him coming up in just a little bit. Did anybody see the video of Nancy Pelosi at, I guess it was a fundraiser that she was doing with Joe Biden? And she went on to talk about how great we are and how I forgot exactly the words because it's hard to do when you're sober to repeat what it was that Nancy Pelosi said. But she basically went on saying how we should be lucky and grateful that we have somebody like Joe Biden as our president. It was, it was an interesting statement. If you see the video and I'll see if I can find the YouTube video and I will post that because it is quite funny. But Nancy Pelosi, she's also out there admitting that the crime surge is absolutely outrageous and it has to be stopped. It's so nice to see that so many of the Democrats are now finally coming around and realizing that, oh my God, we've got a crime wave. Now if they can only realize that part of this crime wave has a lot to do with, oh, what is that thing again? Oh yeah, defunding the police and getting prosecutors in place that don't want to prosecute the criminals. I mean, it's a simple little thing and why some of these people can't do it is amazing. But Nancy Pelosi went to the latest Democrats to jump on board on the recognition that we have a crime way two, three, three, nine, eight, that's the number for the show. Good morning. Welcome to the Brian Rush show. Oops. Sorry. I missed you. But it's kind of funny to see that, especially after all of the crime that was going on in Nancy Pelosi's own backyard. I wonder if she's gonna realize that we do have to actually fund the police and get these prosecutors out that don't want to prosecute crime. I don't know if you saw the latest crime in Chicago, but the Mexican man that was beaten to death while trying to put up his Christmas tree lights. Again, I don't understand why people in Chicago are allowing their city to be run the way they're letting it run. Two, three, three, nine, eight, it's the number. Good morning. Welcome to the Brian Rush Show.",
