    "turn_text": "Under the Trump administration, we got the Mission Act, which specifically pushed the ability to get treated out into the community locally. Our veterans here, if they needed some definitive care beyond what they could get in the local veterans clinic, then they could come downtown and get treated. They didn't have to drive the shans. They didn't have to go to Biloxi. But the VA will tend to capture those guys and force them into the VA system, which means a lot of driving on a lot of commuting. And it's a lot of frustration. So pushing it into the community was a very, very good idea. And that was very popular under the previous administration. Under this administration, that's popular. And of course, we're trying to capture them again. And this goes back to the whole union labor thing, right? The VA health system is very, very, very largely unionized. And so they're capturing those patients and want to hold them in that system. And whereas I don't care one way or",
